  "question": {
    "text": "Two wires of same length and radius are joined end to end and loaded. The Young&#39;s moduli of the materials of the two wires are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The combination behaves as a single wire then its Young&#39;s modulus is:"
  },
